OL,3,GNEWSAThe centuries old-pub game created
OL,4,Aby bored children
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe regular British pub-goer might
OL,7,Fenjoy a throw at a dartboard or a game
OL,8,Fof pool to pass the time in between
OL,9,Fpints.
OL,11,FBut villagers in Stretton, Rutland,
OL,12,Frelish an altogether different kind of
OL,13,Fpub game.
OL,15,FNurdles, or nurdling, involves throwing
OL,16,F13 old pennies into a hole in a pub
OL,17,Fbench, either off a lead backboard or
OL,18,Fstraight in.
OL,23,APub: 29-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
